00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:05.190 align:start position:0%
we want to provide more services that  help people to be as healthy and as well  as they can be and prevent them from  developing health problems this means  services that respond quickly when you  contact them for help it also means  having services that support people in a  holistic way  this means supporting people with things  like housing employment and relationship  problems as well as their emotional and  physical well-being  it includes services that support people  to lead healthier lifestyles for example  to help people stop smoking and lose  weight  we want to give people the skills and  knowledge to be able to help themselves  this is so that they can make healthy  choices lead active lifestyles and reach  up for help and support at the earliest  opportunity  to make this happen we need to make sure  that information about services reaches  as many people as possible  we also want to make sure that services  are welcoming non-judgmental and  sensitive to people's needs and  ambitions  some residents need extra help and  support to access services and  activities that can assist them to  manage their health  in these situations we want people to  know what is available nearby  how to access it and to feel able to  connect into it no matter who they are  or where they live  the gp will often be the first port of  call when someone needs help  yet help can be accessed via other  routes too  our voluntary community  faith and social enterprise sector  partners play a vital role providing a  range of services that support people to  manage their fiscal and mental wellbeing  helping to build resilience and greater  independence
 

